[[:db/retract 17592186153928 :answer-field/choices 17592186153929] [:db/retract 17592186153928 :answer-field/choices 17592186153930] [:db/retract 17592186153928 :answer-field/choices 17592186153931] [:db/retract 17592186153928 :answer-field/choices 17592186153932] [:db/retract 17592186153928 :answer-field/choices 17592186153933] [:db/retract 17592186157615 :question/answer-fields 17592186153934] {:db/id 17592186157614 :question/problem "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v,\\,y=u-{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{3}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v,\\,u-{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1,\\,u-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1,\\,u-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=1,\\,y=u-1,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=1,\\,y(t)=t-1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a vertical line segment with endpoints $(1,0)$ and $(1,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](images/4c/4cda505c17437f64f8ab90dcccca1f55f087af77be6dee0e7c81dbd372760664.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153928 :answer-field/correct "answer-8166063a-dc78-5f3f-8bf7-0c141a4e8d61" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b4e018a-bce1-5b10-a192-2b9d54af71ed" "answer-96d545bf-0741-5454-b677-38f6a4355e5f" "answer-8166063a-dc78-5f3f-8bf7-0c141a4e8d61" "answer-809bfe03-d49c-5afa-b88d-848b85922201" "answer-57862c3c-92cb-58ef-989f-3796b1f3d3f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b4e018a-bce1-5b10-a192-2b9d54af71ed" :answer/id #uuid "2b4e018a-bce1-5b10-a192-2b9d54af71ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1)$ and $(-1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96d545bf-0741-5454-b677-38f6a4355e5f" :answer/id #uuid "96d545bf-0741-5454-b677-38f6a4355e5f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1)$ and $(1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8166063a-dc78-5f3f-8bf7-0c141a4e8d61" :answer/id #uuid "8166063a-dc78-5f3f-8bf7-0c141a4e8d61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0)$ and $(1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-809bfe03-d49c-5afa-b88d-848b85922201" :answer/id #uuid "809bfe03-d49c-5afa-b88d-848b85922201" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0)$ and $(1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57862c3c-92cb-58ef-989f-3796b1f3d3f1" :answer/id #uuid "57862c3c-92cb-58ef-989f-3796b1f3d3f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1)$ and $(1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157615 :question/problem "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,y=-v.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the side ${S}_{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157249 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-015f5e64-8ccf-5a6a-8fbf-8ce2c8d20eda"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-015f5e64-8ccf-5a6a-8fbf-8ce2c8d20eda" :question/id #uuid "015f5e64-8ccf-5a6a-8fbf-8ce2c8d20eda" :question/math-academy-id "q-160631" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=-{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" :question/worked-solution "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u+v,\\,-{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u+0,\\,-{0}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u,\\,0), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u+v,\\,-{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(1+v,\\,-{v}^{2}), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a downward-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(2,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u+v,\\,-{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u+1,\\,-{1}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u+1,\\,-1), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(2,-1)$ to the point $(1,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u+v,\\,-{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0+v,\\,-{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(v,\\,-{v}^{2}), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is a downward-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,-1)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/cc/ccd7576940650b3c1ba7a0b0c404b2dc39d287261d77f556f63b8166496c69df.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d96343de-f671-5ac9-bcd5-9b8c7a8dc39b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d96343de-f671-5ac9-bcd5-9b8c7a8dc39b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d96343de-f671-5ac9-bcd5-9b8c7a8dc39b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afc4090a-a50d-5cfd-b9cf-41e1abf26da6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ba99d86-24e8-5ca6-94cd-b5ea2ff49d0e" "answer-816f6705-f146-5bfb-a96a-c00de5846b39" "answer-69783711-c08d-571c-86a6-8b131065e28d" "answer-afc4090a-a50d-5cfd-b9cf-41e1abf26da6" "answer-2082dc17-8677-5072-8728-eb1279bccdcc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ba99d86-24e8-5ca6-94cd-b5ea2ff49d0e" :answer/id #uuid "8ba99d86-24e8-5ca6-94cd-b5ea2ff49d0e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/3b/3b06791c21bcb41f654c1d01f8e4b9cb58df36cf76615ce0b41a0245835c38d5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-816f6705-f146-5bfb-a96a-c00de5846b39" :answer/id #uuid "816f6705-f146-5bfb-a96a-c00de5846b39" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/72/7215170dcbc618f7a006cc4aedd65bdc36dd8bccd708bbe9784dcbfc4974efea.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69783711-c08d-571c-86a6-8b131065e28d" :answer/id #uuid "69783711-c08d-571c-86a6-8b131065e28d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/86/868f4a5fc5f2e2d30dc5d1a693cb8df7bd6cbdad90483d806a3c08afc521d1ff.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afc4090a-a50d-5cfd-b9cf-41e1abf26da6" :answer/id #uuid "afc4090a-a50d-5cfd-b9cf-41e1abf26da6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cc/ccd7576940650b3c1ba7a0b0c404b2dc39d287261d77f556f63b8166496c69df.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2082dc17-8677-5072-8728-eb1279bccdcc" :answer/id #uuid "2082dc17-8677-5072-8728-eb1279bccdcc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ee/eec7dbae504f01dda802a07eb200fcf9a1823ffd3a71665b87936b24e7e5525a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186373902 :question/problem "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u{v}^{2},\\,y={u}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186290419 :question/problem "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}(v+6u),\\,y=\\frac{{v}^{3}-2u}{v+2}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5d1b8939-e94e-5773-a283-f5d685750aa5" :activity/id #uuid "5d1b8939-e94e-5773-a283-f5d685750aa5" :activity